	(text "NIBBLE BOARD 03 - SEQUENCER: step counter, instruction and operand registers, flags, decoders and the diode control matrix"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 15.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.5 3.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b67bea34-1dfc-4a98-890f-c9b0dc05e391")
	)
	(text "Cell: 2N7000 + 47k pull-up (NMOS, see docs/gate-cell.md).  592 transistors, 354 resistors, 87 matrix diodes, 19 LEDs, 245 x 255 mm (D045).\nFrom the bus header: M7..M0 (the program memory word), CF and ZF (from the ALU), CLK, RST.\nTo the bus header: II, PCE and the matrix columns SUB EO AI AO BI BO BA AB OI IO PCL FI HLT MAI MI MO ONE F0 F1 INP; BUS3#..BUS0# driven (open drain) with OPR3..0 while IO.\nTo the counter cards over the LINK header: OPR7..0, PCR, RAI.  The program counter and the return register live there (D035, D042).\nSteps S0..S4 are a one-hot ring of flip-flops: S0 loads IR/OPR (II), S1 counts (PCE), S2 loads the second word of a jump or call (OPI, PCE), S3 and S4 drive the matrix rows; DONE returns to S0.\ndocs/isa.md is the specification; sim/emu.py the reference the whole-machine simulation checks this board against."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 45.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "e7ab337a-ef61-4912-a3c4-90c346cd14ac")
	)
	(text "THE CONTROL MATRIX"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 574.04 165.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "e154709a-1d1f-4c0a-8573-c7ab3b1120c7")
	)
